From 8ff3b2cbdeb0308998b7a99abc4f56dfa757a37f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jgrizon
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:18:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: wave64 lane reads cross halves on the wave-path
 assumption (off)

The last "a lane read that may cross 32-lane halves" answers are v_readlane_b32
in blocks wave_path says both host waves reach; with VICTORY_WAVE64_REDUCE=1
the read now uses read_lane_across (the halves' own exchange through
threadgroup memory) instead of answering from the reader's half. Same gate as
the reduction and first-lane paths.

Ported from paveledits/ScarlettMac runtime-preview/checkpoint/patches/0015-shader-wave64-lane-reads-cross-halves-on-the-wave-pa.patch

Generated by Mistral Vibe.
Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>
---
 crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs b/crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs
index 6df7a90..3d5c461 100644
--- a/crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs
+++ b/crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs
@@ -7470,6 +7470,20 @@ impl<'a> Lower<'a> {
                             let r = self.read_lane_across(a, lane)?;
                             return int(self, r);
                         }
+                        // Under the reduction switch's wave-path assumption
+                        // both halves reach the exchange's barriers: a lane
+                        // read can cross (`read_lane_across` exchanges the
+                        // halves' own) instead of answering from the reader's.
+                        if wave64_reduce()
+                            && self.cur == self.level
+                            && barriers::wave_path(self.x.p, self.x.st)
+                                .get(self.cur_ir)
+                                .copied()
+                                .unwrap_or(false)
+                        {
+                            let r = self.read_lane_across(a, lane)?;
+                            return int(self, r);
+                        }
                         self.same_half(
                             "a lane read that may cross 32-lane halves (wave64 on a 32-lane host)",
                         )?;
